          "id": "p4-5",
          "speaker": "",
          "text": "The white bear relies on the huge centuries-old trees in the forest in many ways. For example, the old-growth trees have extremely long roots that help prevent erosion of the soil along the banks of the many fish streams."
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-6",
          "speaker": "",
          "text": "Keeping these banks intact is important because these streams are home to salmon, which are the bear’s main food source. In return, the bear’s feeding habits nurture the forest."
